Z||000003||bHooper||01-31-2001||08:52 PM||||where to start?...<P>i got the bright idea that i should try to fix the "lowdest" of the exhaust leaks. after all, it was just a broken bolt!  well,i then managed to strip the head of the other bolt.  and after 2 days of grinding and drilling, i had one out, and a new whole made for the other.<P>i installed new bolts, and what do i have?  puffs of exhaust coming from around the flanges!  arrgh!<P>at this point i decided to tighten the bolts a bit more, and snap!  New broken bolt!  after a hour, that is removed and then i find that i bent the flange on the manifold a bit, preventing the new bolt from going in.<P>no problem, i can reinstall the old bolt.  having that done, and everything tightened to 22 ftlbs, like the good book says, i crank the car.<P>what do i see?  <B>more damn puffs of smoke from around the flanges!</B><P>so, what did i do?  crack the manifolds even more than they were?<P>i am seriously thinking of building an electric powered vehicle!  it may weight 6000 pounds, and go 0-60 in 60 seconds, but at least there won't be <B>any</B> exhaust manifolds!<P>thanks for listening!<P>hoop||||reg||1
Z||000004||black-86-GT||01-31-2001||09:40 PM||||thats exactly what i said when i almost sliced my thumb off from a bolt breaking on the front manifold. be careful and good luck||||reg||1
Z||000005||Tina||01-31-2001||11:07 PM||||Be careful!!<BR>ALWAYS disconnect battery before working<BR>on your Fiero.<BR>It can hear you otherwise.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Oh,and good luck<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tina.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||GT Bastard||02-01-2001||01:17 AM||||By now, you could have pulled the heads and given them to a machine shop.  That's what I did.  That'll give you an excuse to have the heads ported and freshened up.  Go for it!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/gtbastard.gif">  <P>Only dead fish swim with the stream.||||reg||1
Z||000007||bHooper||02-01-2001||03:05 PM||||well, bastard  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">, but finding someone around here that knows how to do anything at all like that is like finding a lepur with an oposible thumb still atached!<P>drove the car to work, this morning, and the loudest part of the exhaust leak is gone, but there is a lot more of a tic tic sound!<P>hoop||||reg||1
Z||000008||bHooper||02-20-2001||09:50 PM||||son of a monkey's unkle!!  gosh darn, frikin manifolds!!!!!!<P>so Ed Parks sends me a repaired front manifold... i spend saturday removing the old one, and sunday installing the new.<P>today, i finish up the job, reinstalling the heat shields battery, etc.<P>fire (that's really not a good word to use around these cars is it?)... crank it up, and what do i hear.... tick tick tick!!! aaghh!<P>so, i start feeling around everywhere, and wouldn't you know it?  the rear manifold has a <B>new</B> crack in it the size of my @$$!!<P>tickticktickticktickticktickticktickticktick!<P>me not happy!<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT<BR>KYB's, Eibach's,<BR>Poly Bushings||||reg||1
